# Start this IOC

This directory contains two alternative startup files for one IOC.
Run one at a time. Both enable linStat, autosave and retools.

Open Bash and activate the EPICS tree used to generate this project:

```bash
source "_EPICS_BASE_/../setEpicsEnv.bash"
cd "_TOP_/iocBoot/_IOC_"
```

Start the loader directly, without building the application:

```bash
./st.loader.cmd
```

It loads module support from the selected tree and reads application inputs
from `_TOP_/_APPNAME_App/Db` and `_TOP_/_APPNAME_App/iocsh`.
Keep additional `module` directives in `st.loader.cmd`, not in nested files.

To inspect resolved module support without starting the IOC:

```bash
iocsh.bash --show st.loader.cmd
```

To use the compiled application, build first and run its startup:

```bash
make -C "_TOP_"
./st.cmd
```

Select support in `configure/RELEASE` and `_APPNAME_App/src/Makefile`.
The compiled startup reads application inputs installed under `db/` and
`iocsh/`. Both startups load `_APPNAME_.iocsh` with `DATABASE_TOP` pointing
at their respective database directory. Configure device-specific inputs
in that application fragment.

Enter `exit` at the IOC prompt to stop it. Initialization alone does not
verify device communication.

## Runtime files

Both startups change the working directory to `_TOP_` before loading services.
Autosave uses `var/autosave/<IOCNAME>/{req,save}`; diagnostic files use
`var/epics-pvinfo/{env,names}`. These directories are created at startup.
The first launch has no saved values to restore; later launches can restore
values tagged with autosave DB info.

Override the roots before starting either file:

```bash
export AS_TOP=/path/to/writable/autosave
export TARGET_TOP=/path/to/writable/diagnostics
```

Relative roots resolve from `_TOP_`. Preparation writes the absolute autosave
root to `epics-pvinfo/env/<IOCNAME>.paths.iocsh`; startup imports it before
calling commonIocsh. This also supports relative names beginning with a hyphen.
Autosave paths may contain ASCII
letters, digits, underscore, dot, slash and hyphen; other bytes are rejected
because the installed fragment passes that path to a shell command.
TARGET_TOP holds the `epics-pvinfo` directory.

Before initialization, startup requires the default linStat host/process and
autosave status records. Missing records stop startup even when a nested
fragment continues after a database load error. These presence checks do not
verify every field, optional record or later device operation.

With ioc-runner, select `st.cmd` or `st.loader.cmd` explicitly in the IOC
configuration. Both files are executable, so do not rely on an automatic
choice when generating that configuration.

## Optional shared services

Default startups enable `linStat`, `autosave` and `retools`. Optional
`commonIocsh` fragments are configured before `iocInit` in `st.cmd` (after
enabling the corresponding module in `configure/RELEASE` and rebuilding) or in
`st.loader.cmd` (after adding the top-level `module` directive):

- Optional `linStat` interface and filesystem checks:

```iocsh
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/linStat.iocsh", "IOC=$(IOCNAME),NICENABLE=,NIC=eth0,FSENABLE=,FSID=DATA,DIR=$(TOP)")
```

- `iocStatsAdmin` (alternative to `linStat` host/process statistics; uncomment
  `devIocStats = $(MODULES)/iocStats` in `configure/RELEASE` or add
  `module iocStats` in `st.loader.cmd`, and disable `linStat.iocsh` together
  with its `HOST_SCAN`/`PROCESS_ID` `dbpr` checks):

```iocsh
# Compiled startup (st.cmd):
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/iocStatsAdmin.iocsh", "IOC=$(IOCNAME)")

# Loader startup (st.loader.cmd):
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/iocStatsAdmin.iocsh", "IOC=$(IOCNAME),devIocStats=$(IOCSTATS)")
```

  Startup validation in `prepare-runtime.bash` stops before `iocInit` if
  `iocStatsAdmin` is selected with an `IOC` prefix exceeding 21 characters or
  combined with `linStat`, `linStatHost` or `linStatProc` under the same prefix.

- `reccaster` (`RECCASTER = $(MODULES)/recsync` in `configure/RELEASE` or
  `module recsync` in `st.loader.cmd`):

```iocsh
# Compiled startup (st.cmd):
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/reccaster.iocsh", "IOC=$(IOCNAME)")

# Loader startup (st.loader.cmd):
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/reccaster.iocsh", "IOC=$(IOCNAME),RECCASTER=$(RECSYNC)")
```

- External logging (`iocLog.iocsh` uses Base; `caPutLog.iocsh` requires
  `CAPUTLOG = $(MODULES)/caPutLog` or `module caPutLog` plus an access-security
  file with `TRAPWRITE` loaded before `iocInit`):

```iocsh
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/iocLog.iocsh", "IOC=$(IOCNAME),LOG_INET=127.0.0.1,LOG_INET_PORT=7004")
asSetFilename("$(DB_TOP)/accessSecurityFile.acf")
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/caPutLog.iocsh", "LOG_INET=127.0.0.1,LOG_INET_PORT=7004,OPTION=0")
```

- Optional serial configuration (`ASYN = $(MODULES)/asyn` or `module asyn`;
  create the port inside the application config before calling
  `setSerialParams.iocsh`):

```iocsh
iocshLoad("$(IOCSH_TOP)/iocsh/serial.iocsh", "SERIAL_ENABLE=,SERIAL_CONFIG=$(IOCSH_LOCAL_TOP)/serial-ports.iocsh")
```
